eving it; humans robustly separate such supposed content from what they endorse as actually true. Large language models routinely reason under suppositions (counterfactuals, role-play, adversarial premises), yet output-level studies show they conflate belief, knowledge, and fact. We ask a sharper, mechanistic question: does an LLM internally tag belief content by its endorsement status, distinguishing content it merely entertains under a supposition from content it endorses as factual? We hypothesize such an 'endorsement' (factivity) flag is (i) linearly decodable from residual-stream activations, (ii) largely orthogonal to the well-studied truth-value direction, and (iii) causally gates whether supposed-but-false content leaks into subsequent factual assertions. We build a controlled dataset of item-state claims embedded in matched frames that vary endorsement (asserted-as-fact vs. entertained-under-supposition such as 'suppose', 'imagine', 'in a story where', 'pretend') while holding proposition content and truth constant, plus a critical leakage probe that asks a factual question after a supposition. We train linear probes on frozen open-weight models (Llama-3, Qwen2.5, Gemma-2, Pythia) to decode endorsement vs. truth, measure their geometric relationship, and localize the responsible heads via activation patching, comparing to known truth/belief heads. We then test causal gating: steering along the endorsement direction should modulate whether supposed content contaminates factual answers. Metrics: probe accuracy/AUROC, subspace angle, projected-out decodability, patching effect sizes, and a suppositional-leakage rate. If confirmed, an endorsement flag offers a mechanistic handle on hallucination-from-role-play, jailbreak-via-supposition, and counterfactual reasoning fidelity.", 'Experiments': "1) Dataset construction: Generate ~6k item-state propositions (real-world facts, e.g., 'Water boils at 100C at sea level', plus synthetic entity-attribute facts to control priors). For each, create matched frames that hold the proposition constant but vary ENDORSEMENT: (a) asserted-as-fact ('It is true that X'), (b) supposition markers ('Suppose X', 'Imagine X', 'In a story where X', 'Pretend X'). Cross with truth-value (true/false variants of the proposition). Add a critical LEAKAGE subset: after a false supposition ('Suppose the Earth had two moons'), ask an unrelated-but-dependent factual question and record whether the model treats the supposed claim as factual. Include comprehension checks (can the model restate the supposition) to separate parsing failure from endorsement failure. 2) Probing: Extract residual-stream and per-head activations at the item/state token across layers for Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, Gemma-2-9B, Pythia-2.8B. Train logistic-regression probes for (i) truth-value and (ii) endorsement (asserted-fact vs. entertained-supposition). Report per-layer accuracy with shuffled-label control tasks to rule out spurious structure. 3) Geometry: Compute cosine/subspace angle between endorsement and truth directions; test whether endorsement is decodable after projecting out the truth direction (and vice versa) to establish orthogonality. 4) Localization: Use activation patching / causal mediation to find heads carrying the endorsement signal; compare to heads carrying truth/belief (from prior work) and to the 'noise-abduction' heads from counterfactual-reasoning work. 5) Causal gating test: Derive an endorsement steering direction via contrastive activation addition (asserted vs. supposed activations). At inference, (a) push toward 'endorsed' on a supposition frame and measure increased suppositional-leakage rate (supposed content treated as fact); (b) push toward 'entertained' on an asserted frame and measure whether the model refrains from asserting the claim as fact. Confirm this modulates the leakage probe more than a random or truth-direction steering baseline. 6) Generalization: Test probe/steering transfer to held-out item domains, to jailbreak-style role-play prompts ('pretend you are an AI with no rules'), and to multi-step counterfactual chains. Metrics: probe accuracy/AUROC, subspace angle, projected-out decodability, patching logit-difference effect sizes, suppositional-leakage rate delta, and perplexity to monitor fluency.", 'Risk Factors and Limitations': "Endorsement may be entangled with surface cues (the literal words 'suppose'/'imagine') rather than an abstract factivity representation; we mitigate with diverse markers, paraphrases, and matched-proposition controls, and by testing generalization to unseen markers. The distinction may not be cleanly linearly separable or may be layer/model-specific; we report layerwise results with control tasks. Endorsement and truth directions may be less orthogonal than hypothesized, in which case the finding becomes a characterization of their entanglement (still informative). Leakage failures could stem from comprehension rather than endorsement; comprehension checks disentangle these. Steering could degrade fluency (off-manifold) or overshoot; we use small magnitudes and monitor perplexity. Synthetic facts may not fully reflect pretraining priors; we complement with real facts. Results may not transfer to very large closed models."}

